I've read in this group about ttyrec files that record people's games
but I've never looked at one until just recently.

It was very eye opening.  I went to
http://www.mindspring.com/~jove/Ttyrecs.htm and followed the links to
the first files for Marvin, as an Elven Priestess.

The thing that really stands out is how efficient he was moving all of
his stuff down through the dungeons.  He made a couple of trips back up
to a shop and such, but generally he moved down through the dungeon
once and then out!  I'm always going up and down and that is one reason
why my ascensions take so long.  Prior to this I've been making a big
stash near an altar and going back up to it to over and over again.
I'm thinking of trying to move all my stuff down with me next time I
play.  I have a game in progress and I'm trying  it out now.  It is a
little tedious dragging all my stuff down the stairs but I just found
and altar and have gotten everything's B/U/C status and gotten MJ (I'm
a Valkarie).

In Marvin's game he had a blessed bag of holding and gauntlets of power
so he could carry a ton of stuff.  My theory is to just leave things on
the down stairs, maybe with the E word on the square and keep moving
the pile down until I can carry more stuff.

Anyway, there were a lot more tactics and such as well that I didn't
know as well.  It was definately a great way to be spoiled.  Can't say
I can apply everything I saw as efficiently, but I'm sure it will help.

My theory is that nethack will be more fun if the games are shorter.
The game I have in progress was supposed to be with conducts - no
polypile, geno, wishes - but I think that would just make my game
longer and more tedious - I'm really cautious and usually way
overprepared when I ascend.  So, I'm thinking of changing courses and
going for shorter, less cautious games applying some of what I've
learned.

Also very interesting was how Marvin handled the levels under the
castle.  He skipped a lot of the mazes and fought his way through with
a silver dagger!  I guess you don't need a silver saber or an artifact
with cold or lightning damage in the end game.

